{"op": "task_created", "id": "project-skeleton", "title": "Cargo project skeleton", "description": "Create examples/rust-cli as a cargo project: Cargo.toml (package rcli, edition 2021, lib + bin), src/lib.rs, src/main.rs (placeholder main returning 0), tests/ dir, fixtures/ dir. .gitignore must ignore ONLY build output with root-anchored patterns: /target (bare 'target' would also match any source dir named target).", "acceptance": ["Cargo.toml declares package rcli with edition 2021 and both lib and bin targets", ".gitignore contains /target and no bare patterns that could match source directories", "cargo build produces a runnable rcli binary"], "files": ["Cargo.toml", "src/lib.rs", "src/main.rs", "tests/.gitkeep", "fixtures/.gitkeep", ".gitignore"], "priority": "high", "notes": [], "seq": 1, "ts": "2026-08-07T08:39:52+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "cargo-build", "title": "Build/test pipeline green with zero warnings", "description": "Ensure `cargo build` and `cargo test` work end to end with no compiler warnings (rustc warnings are on by default). The bin target must have a --help that prints usage and exits 0. Keep Cargo.lock committed (binary crate).", "acceptance": ["cargo build succeeds with zero warnings", "cargo test succeeds (may be empty initially)", "rcli --help exits 0 and prints usage", "Cargo.lock is committed"], "files": ["Cargo.toml", "src/main.rs", "Cargo.lock"], "priority": "high", "notes": [], "seq": 2, "ts": "2026-08-07T08:39:52+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "error-def", "title": "RcliError enum with Display", "description": "src/error.rs: enum RcliError { Io(std::io::Error), Parse { line: usize, col: usize, msg: String }, Empty, Usage(String) }. Implement std::error::Error + Display with clear messages ('rcli: <msg>' not included - main adds the prefix; Display renders 'line L, column C: msg' for Parse). From<std::io::Error> impl. Public re-export from lib.rs.", "acceptance": ["RcliError::Parse renders 'line 3, column 5: ...'", "From<io::Error> conversion works", "error module compiles standalone"], "files": ["src/error.rs", "src/lib.rs"], "priority": "high", "notes": [], "seq": 3, "ts": "2026-08-07T08:39:52+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "csv-parser", "title": "CSV parser with quoted fields and positioned errors", "description": "src/csv.rs: pub fn parse(input: &str) -> Result<Vec<Vec<String>>, RcliError>. Rules: comma-separated fields, double-quoted fields may contain commas, newlines are NOT allowed inside quoted fields (error), \"\" inside a quoted field is an escaped quote, CRLF and LF both accepted as row terminators, trailing newline optional, blank lines skipped. Track line and column for errors. Unclosed quote at end of input -> Parse error at its position.", "acceptance": ["parse(\"a,b\\nc,d\") -> [[a,b],[c,d]]", "quoted field with comma stays one field: \"x,y\"", "escaped quotes: \"say \"\"hi\"\"\" -> say \"hi\"", "unclosed quote -> Parse error with line and column", "CRLF input parses identically to LF"], "files": ["src/csv.rs", "src/lib.rs"], "priority": "high", "notes": [], "seq": 4, "ts": "2026-08-07T08:39:52+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "csv-parser-tests", "title": "CSV parser unit tests", "description": "tests/csv_tests.rs (or #[cfg(test)] mod in csv.rs - prefer integration tests under tests/): table of cases: basic rows, quoted commas, escaped quotes, empty fields (a,,b), trailing newline, no trailing newline, CRLF, blank lines skipped, unclosed quote error with position, empty input -> Empty error.", "acceptance": ["all csv parser cases pass under cargo test", "error cases assert exact line/column", "cargo test reports the suite by name"], "files": ["tests/csv_tests.rs"], "priority": "medium", "notes": [], "seq": 5, "ts": "2026-08-07T08:39:52+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "stats-engine", "title": "Per-column stats engine", "description": "src/stats.rs: pub struct ColumnStats { name: String, count: usize, numeric: usize, sum: Option<f64>, mean: Option<f64>, median: Option<f64>, min: Option<f64>, max: Option<f64> }. pub fn column_stats(rows: &[Vec<String>], col: usize) -> ColumnStats. count = non-empty cells; numeric fields parsed as f64 (trimmed); non-numeric cells excluded from sum/mean/median/min/max but counted in count; a column with no numeric cells -> all Option fields None. pub fn stats_all(rows: &[Vec<String>], header: &[String]) -> Vec<ColumnStats> (uses header names, or 'col N' when header shorter).", "acceptance": ["column [1,2,3,4] -> count 4, sum 10, mean 2.5, median 2.5, min 1, max 4", "column [1,x,3] -> count 3, numeric 2, mean 2", "column [a,b] -> all numeric stats None", "empty rows -> count 0, stats None"], "files": ["src/stats.rs", "src/lib.rs"], "priority": "high", "notes": [], "seq": 6, "ts": "2026-08-07T08:39:52+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "stats-engine-tests", "title": "Stats engine unit tests", "description": "tests/stats_tests.rs: known-value cases: even-count median, odd-count median (middle value), all-numeric column, mixed column, empty column, single row, header longer than data rows, negative numbers, decimals.", "acceptance": ["median of [1,2,3] is 2 (odd)", "median of [1,2,3,4] is 2.5 (even)", "mixed/empty columns produce None numeric stats", "all cases green under cargo test"], "files": ["tests/stats_tests.rs"], "priority": "medium", "notes": [], "seq": 7, "ts": "2026-08-07T08:39:52+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "describe", "title": "Describe subcommand logic", "description": "src/describe.rs: pub fn describe(rows: &[Vec<String>], header: &[String]) -> String. Output format (one line per column): 'name: rows=N non_empty=M type=numeric|string|mixed|empty'. type is numeric if every non-empty cell parses as f64, string if none parse, mixed otherwise, empty if no non-empty cells. Include a trailing summary line 'file: R data rows, C columns'.", "acceptance": ["numeric column reports type=numeric", "mixed column reports type=mixed", "empty file reports 0 data rows", "output is deterministic (stable ordering)"], "files": ["src/describe.rs", "src/lib.rs"], "priority": "medium", "notes": [], "seq": 8, "ts": "2026-08-07T08:39:52+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "head", "title": "Head subcommand logic", "description": "src/head.rs: pub fn head(rows: &[Vec<String>], header: &[String], n: usize) -> String. Renders header + first n rows as re-quoted CSV (fields containing comma/quote/newline get quoted, quotes doubled). n=0 -> header only. n >= rows -> all rows. Negative n -> treat as 0. Trailing newline after last line.", "acceptance": ["head with n=2 returns header + 2 rows", "n=0 returns header only", "n larger than row count returns all rows", "re-quoting round-trips: re-parsing head output equals original prefix"], "files": ["src/head.rs", "src/lib.rs"], "priority": "medium", "notes": [], "seq": 9, "ts": "2026-08-07T08:39:52+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "cli-args", "title": "Hand-rolled CLI argument parsing", "description": "src/cli.rs: pub enum Command { Stats(PathBuf), Describe(PathBuf), Head { path: PathBuf, n: usize } }. pub fn parse_args(args: &[String]) -> Result<Command, RcliError>. Accepts 'stats <file>', 'describe <file>', 'head <file> [-n N]' (default N=10). Unknown subcommand -> RcliError::Usage('unknown subcommand ...'), missing file arg -> Usage, '-n' without value -> Usage, negative/zero -n -> Usage. Also '--help'/'help' handled by main, not here.", "acceptance": ["parse(['stats','f.csv']) -> Stats(f.csv)", "parse(['head','f.csv','-n','2']) -> Head n=2", "parse(['frobnicate','x']) -> Usage error", "parse(['stats']) -> Usage error (missing path)"], "files": ["src/cli.rs", "src/lib.rs"], "priority": "high", "notes": [], "seq": 10, "ts": "2026-08-07T08:39:52+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "main-wiring", "title": "main.rs dispatch, error rendering, exit codes", "description": "src/main.rs: parse env args (skip argv[0]) via cli::parse_args; on Usage error print 'rcli: <msg>' to stderr plus 'try: rcli --help' and exit 2; on other errors print 'rcli: <msg>' to stderr and exit 1; success prints result to stdout and exits 0. Commands: read file (io error -> RcliError::Io), parse csv, dispatch to stats_all/describe/head and print. --help prints usage and exits 0. Stats output format: 'name: count=N sum=.. mean=.. median=.. min=.. max=..' with %.6g-style formatting (Rust '{}' on f64 is fine), n/a for None.", "acceptance": ["rcli stats fixtures/numbers.csv prints expected per-column lines", "missing file -> stderr 'rcli: ...' and exit 1", "unknown subcommand -> exit 2 with usage hint", "--help exits 0"], "files": ["src/main.rs"], "priority": "high", "notes": [], "seq": 11, "ts": "2026-08-07T08:39:52+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "fixtures", "title": "Fixture CSV files", "description": "fixtures/: numbers.csv (header + 5 numeric rows incl. negative and decimal), mixed.csv (numeric + string + empty cells), quoted.csv (fields with commas and escaped quotes), empty.csv (zero bytes), header-only.csv (one header row, no data), crlf.csv (CRLF line endings).", "acceptance": ["each fixture parses with csv::parse without error (except empty.csv -> Empty)", "fixtures cover numeric, mixed, quoted, empty, header-only, CRLF cases"], "files": ["fixtures/numbers.csv", "fixtures/mixed.csv", "fixtures/quoted.csv", "fixtures/empty.csv", "fixtures/header-only.csv", "fixtures/crlf.csv"], "priority": "low", "notes": [], "seq": 12, "ts": "2026-08-07T08:39:52+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "cli-tests", "title": "CLI integration tests (real binary)", "description": "tests/cli_tests.rs: invoke the built binary via std::process::Command (env CARGO_BIN_EXE_rcli is set by cargo test for integration tests). Cases: stats on numbers.csv contains 'mean=3' etc; head -n 2 on quoted.csv round-trips; describe on mixed.csv reports type=mixed; missing file -> exit code 1 and stderr starts with 'rcli:'; unknown subcommand -> exit 2; --help -> exit 0.", "acceptance": ["CARGO_BIN_EXE_rcli used (no hardcoded paths)", "exit codes asserted: 0 success, 1 data/io error, 2 usage", "stderr content asserted for error cases", "all cases green under cargo test"], "files": ["tests/cli_tests.rs"], "priority": "medium", "notes": [], "seq": 13, "ts": "2026-08-07T08:39:52+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "edge-cases", "title": "Edge-case and stress tests", "description": "tests/edge_cases.rs: header-only file (stats -> zero data rows, all n/a), file with only commas, single-column file, quoted field that looks numeric (\"123\" -> string), unicode column names, very long single line (10k chars), no trailing newline, 1000-row file parses, negative numbers in quotes, empty input -> Empty error propagates as exit 1 via CLI.", "acceptance": ["all edge cases produce correct output or clean errors", "no panics on pathological input (test asserts no panic via process exit)", "1000-row parse completes"], "files": ["tests/edge_cases.rs"], "priority": "medium", "notes": [], "seq": 14, "ts": "2026-08-07T08:39:52+00:00", "v": 1}
